Comment: I think we could still use this, but fix it:

`if: github.event_name == 'push' || (github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name != github.repository)`

So:
- If a push, run
- If a pull request and not from internal, run

So forks should still run on a push to themselves.  We should run on pushes internally.  We should also have a run on a pull request, but from a fork.  Right?  Does that make logical sense?

