comment:
The `FinalizationRegistry` is currently only logging a message but not actually dumping the body when the `returnValue` is garbage collected. This defeats the purpose of the registry as a cleanup mechanism. 

Consider updating the callback to actually perform the cleanup:

```javascript
const registry = new FinalizationRegistry(() => {
  logger.debug('🦔', 'Body not consumed, dumping');
  // Can't use await in FinalizationRegistry callback
  result.body.dump().catch(e => 
    logger.error('Failed to dump body during finalization', e)
  );
});
```

Note that `await` can't be used directly in a FinalizationRegistry callback, so the promise needs to be handled with `.catch()` to prevent unhandled rejections.
```suggestion
    const registry = new FinalizationRegistry(() => {
        logger.debug('🦔', 'Body not consumed, dumping')
        result.body.dump().catch(e => 
            logger.error('Failed to dump body during finalization', e)
        )
    })
    registry.register(returnValue, undefined)
```


