This change removes the special handling for external URLs. The original code used `window.open(href, '_blank')` for URLs starting with 'https://', but now all hrefs are passed to `router.actions.push()`, which is designed for internal navigation only.

While this works for removing the MCP Server link specifically, it breaks the general capability to handle external links in the tree. Consider either:

1. Restoring the external link handling logic:
```javascript
if (typeof href === 'string' && href.startsWith('https://')) {
    window.open(href, '_blank')
} else {
    router.actions.push(href)
}
```

2. Or ensuring that external links are properly handled wherever the MCP Server link is being moved to.

This maintains backward compatibility for any other external links that might exist or be added in the future.
